==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tréyes}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|testifien}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|testifier}}, from {{der|en|la|testificārī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|testificor||I bear witness}}, from {{m|la|testis||a witness}} + {{m|la|facere||to make}}. See {{af|en|-fy|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛstɪfaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-testify.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|tes|ti|fy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|ambitransitive}}

# To make a [[declaration]], or give [[evidence]], under [[oath]].
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=w:Ruzwana Bashir|title=The untold story of how a culture of shame perpetuates abuse. I know, I was a victim|url=http://www.theguardian.com/society/2014/aug/29/-sp-untold-story-culture-of-shame-ruzwana-bashir|date=29 August 2014|passage=It was only after a decade away from Skipton that I was finally able to garner the courage to return and '''testify''' against my abuser.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Numbers|35|30|passage=One witness shall not '''testify''' against any person to cause him to die.}}
# To make a [[statement]] based on [[personal]] [[knowledge]] or [[faith]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|John|3|11|passage=We speak that we do know, and '''testify''' that we have seen; and ye receive not our witness.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Tho[mas] Allen|chapter=Jesus Christ’s Sixth Royal Embassy; or Word to the Angel of the Church in Philadelphia|title=The Christian’s Sure Guide to Eternal Glory: Or, Living Oracles Most Comfortable, Holy and Instructive of the Lord Jesus Christ from Heaven, in His Royal Embassy to the Seven Churches of Asia,{{nb...|as Deliver’d to St. John after His Glorification. Containing, I. The Names and Titles wherewith He was, is, and must be Ever Honoured in Glory. II. The Comforts and Instructions which All Churches Need for Their Increase in Faith and Holiness. III. The Wonderful Large and Gracious Promises of Eternal Life to Encourage All Men to Persevere and Conquer. IV. Prayers and Suitable Devotions to Render the Whole Most Useful and Acceptable.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} Francis Jefferies{{nb...|at the Bible and Crown, in Ludgate-street.}}|year=1733|page=253|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DD5VAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA253|oclc=644249695|passage=[T]he pleaſures of ſenſe have no reliſh vvhere thou &#91;{{w|Jesus}}&#93; irradiateſt and '''teſtifieſt''' vvith our conſcience, that vve are the children of God, and have done thy vvill ſincerely, {{...}}}}

